h2. Test Metrics Without Feature Files

h4. Traditional BDD Challenge
Tools parse .feature files to generate test counts and reports, but this creates maintenance overhead.

h4. Our Solution
*Automated metric extraction directly from test code:*

{code:python}
@allure.feature('User Management')
@allure.story('Login')
@pytest.mark.smoke
def test_user_login():
    with allure.step("Given: User on login page"):
        # Implementation
    with allure.step("When: User enters credentials"):
        # Implementation  
    with allure.step("Then: User sees dashboard"):
        # Implementation
{code}

*Generates:*
* Test inventory reports (JSON/HTML)
* Count by feature, severity, priority
* Real-time metrics during CI/CD
* Integration with dashboards

{tip}*Advantage*: Single source of truth, no file synchronization issues{tip}

